From: Doruk Aktun <info@dorukaktun.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: initialise the completion of every master

cci_reset() always waits on master[0].irq_complete, and cci_isr()
completes master[0] (and master[1] when it exists) on a reset ack.
The completions are only initialised for the masters that have a child
node in DT, so a board that only describes i2c-bus@1 makes the first
cci_reset() in probe dereference an uninitialised wait queue:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000000
  pc : wait_for_completion_timeout+0xb0/0x184
  Call trace:
   wait_for_completion_timeout+0xb0/0x184 (P)
   cci_probe+0x374/0x54c [i2c_qcom_cci]
   platform_probe+0x5c/0xa4

The oops happens with the wait queue lock held and interrupts off. When
udev loads the module at boot the machine then stops responding.

Initialise the completion of every master the controller has before
parsing the child nodes.

Seen on the Razer Edge (SM8350), whose front camera sits on CCI1 master 1.

Fixes: e517526195de ("i2c: Add Qualcomm CCI I2C driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
index 873e901a2..5bf77f14b 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -520,6 +520,13 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!cci->data)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
+	/*
+	 * cci_reset() waits on master[0] and cci_isr() completes it, whether
+	 * or not master 0 is described in DT: initialise every master.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < cci->data->num_masters; i++)
+		init_completion(&cci->master[i].irq_complete);
+
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(dev->of_node, child) {
 		struct cci_master *master;
 		u32 idx;
@@ -558,8 +565,6 @@ static int cci_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			else if (val == I2C_MAX_FAST_MODE_PLUS_FREQ)
 				master->mode = I2C_MODE_FAST_PLUS;
 		}
-
-		init_completion(&master->irq_complete);
 	}
 
 	/* Memory */
-- 
